# Build output
/bin/
/latem
/dist/
*.test
*.out

# Coverage
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Local agent state — never commit anything from a real ~/.latem
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sock
agent.key
secrets.env

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Go workspace files are per-developer
go.work
go.work.sum

# The reference Expo app (examples/expo-app) is a real, buildable app, so it
# drags in the whole JS/iOS toolchain's output. What is committed is the source,
# app.json, eas.json, the lockfiles, and ci/ — everything below is regenerated
# by `pnpm install` and `expo prebuild`.
node_modules/
.expo/
*.ipa
*.app.zip
# Build output for the example apps: .app bundles, .xcarchive, DerivedData, the
# exported ipa, and Gradle's apk/aab all land here. Scoped to examples/ so it
# cannot swallow a directory called build/ elsewhere in the tree.
examples/*/build/
examples/*/*/build/

# Gradle. .gradle/ is per-project daemon and cache state; local.properties
# records this machine's SDK path and must never be committed — a runner would
# inherit a path that does not exist on it. ci/lib/env.sh sets ANDROID_HOME
# instead, which is the reproducible form.
.gradle/
local.properties
# The wrapper JAR is committed on purpose: ./gradlew must work on a fresh clone
# with no Gradle installed, which is exactly what a runner has every run (§12).
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
# `expo prebuild` generates ios/ and android/ from app.json. Committing them is
# a supported Expo workflow ("bare"), but it means app.json stops being the
# source of truth and every SDK upgrade becomes a manual merge. Keep them
# generated; ci/install.sh runs prebuild.
examples/expo-app/ios/
examples/expo-app/android/
# Fastlane's per-run output, not its config. Fastfile/Appfile/Matchfile are
# committed; these three are logs, temp keys, and a local state cache.
# NOTE THE **/ PREFIX. A gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so `fastlane/report.xml` would match only
# <root>/fastlane/ and never examples/ios-native/fastlane/ — which is the only
# place these files actually appear. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
#
# fastlane/metadata/ is the Android changelog tree: ci/android/build.sh writes it
# per run keyed by versionCode and removes it on exit, so ignoring it means a
# killed run cannot leave a stray changelog to be committed.
**/fastlane/metadata/
**/fastlane/report.xml
**/fastlane/Preview.html
**/fastlane/test_output/
# Bundler installs gems here when configured with --path; the Gemfile and
# Gemfile.lock are what pin versions.
#
# `vendor/bundle/` alone does NOT work: a pattern with an internal slash is
# anchored to the directory holding this file, so it matched only <root>/vendor/
# while the gems actually live in examples/*/vendor/bundle/ — about 9,000 files
# that `git add .` would have happily staged. `.bundle/` works by accident,
# because a pattern whose only slash is trailing matches at any depth.
.bundle/
**/vendor/bundle/
